 ===============================================================================
  Center-of-mass information for GNSS satellites                                
 ===============================================================================
                                                                                
 Notes:                                                                         
                                                                                
   - All coordinates refer to the IGS conventions of the spacecraft body axis   
     orientations as defined in Ref. [CM01]                                     
   - CoM hisotry of QZSS satellites is based on BoL/EoL mass and CoM values from
     [CM07,09,10,11] and current mass values according to                       
                                                                                
       mu(t) = (m(t) - m(EoL))/m(EoL)                                           
                                                                                
       dCoG = (CoG(BoL)-CoG(EoL))/(mu(BoL)*(1-mu(BoL)))                         
                                                                                
       CoG(t) = CoG(EoL) + dCoG * mu(t)*(1-mu(t))                               
                                                                                
 References:                                                                    
                                                                                
   [CM01]  Montenbruck O, Schmid R, Mercier F, Steigenberger P, Noll C,         
           Fatkulin R, Kogure S, Ganeshan AS (2015) GNSS satellite geometry and 
           attitude models. Adv Space Res 56(6): 1015-1029,                     
           doi: 10.1016/j.asr.2015.06.019                                                                                 
                                                                                
